{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "3005d495-896b-82bc-87ac-e78e6d59bccc",
  "created_at": "2026-01-12T12:20:55-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Terrence E. Donovan",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:17:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:17:33-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hello. Afternoon. I've got a tree limb down, or half down, and I'm not sure who I'm supposed to call about it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:17:42-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can help with that. Where is it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:17:46-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One eighty-four Bacheller Street. Fifth Ward. Well, it's by there. It's not on my property, I'm the neighbor. It's the tree next door."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:17:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And what's it doing, is it blocking the road or the sidewalk?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:18:01-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] It's hanging over the sidewalk. Big limb, cracked off and caught up in the branches. It's about head height at the low end. Nobody's going to walk under it if they've got any sense, but people do."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:18:16-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's not good. When did it come down?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:18:20-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The storm. Friday into Saturday, the coastal one. I figured somebody would've come by since. Two days now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:18:28-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Crews have been swamped since that storm, a lot of calls. So here's how it works. If the tree is in the city right-of-way, like a street tree, we take it. If it's on private property, it's the owner's responsibility, even if the limb is over the sidewalk. And if it's tangled in wires, that's the utility, and you'd want to keep clear of it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:18:52-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No wires on it that I can see. Just the one pole across the way. So how do I know whose tree it is?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:02-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Is it between the sidewalk and the street, or back toward the house?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Back toward the house. Inside the fence line, more or less. The trunk's in their yard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:15-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So that's theirs, then."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:17-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Most likely private, yes. But I'll log it so someone can look at the sidewalk side, and if they find it's ours, they'll deal with it. Do you know if the owner's home?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:30-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Don't think so. Haven't seen anybody since the storm. Place is quiet. I'd knock but I'm not going to be hollering at an empty house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:40-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. Can I get a name and number in case the inspector has questions?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:46-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Terrence Donovan. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-five-five."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:19:49-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Terrence Donovan, five-five-five, oh-one-five-five. Great. In the meantime, if you've got cones or tape, or even a chair, you could mark off under it. Don't try to pull it down yourself."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:01-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm seventy-some. I'm not pulling anything down. I'll put a couple of trash cans out there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:08-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. And if it comes down on the sidewalk or into the street, call back right away and we'll treat it as a hazard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Should've been told that's how it goes, honestly. I'd have called Saturday. I always figure the city just handles trees."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:27-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Only the ones on city land. It confuses a lot of people."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:32-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well. I've got to get going anyway. Friday's lottery tickets I buy out of habit, and I forgot last week, so I'm not letting that happen twice. Funny, the one week I skip, there's a storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, maybe next Friday. We'll get that logged for you, Mr. Donovan."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:51-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Appreciate it. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:20:53-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Take care."
    }
  ],
